      intro: 'New Port Richey is home. Fly Visuals is based at 8132 Cormel St — where we design, print, and install every vehicle wrap, sign, graphic, and window tint serving Pasco County. Local customers get the shortest turnaround and the most direct service of anyone we work with.',
      local1: 'From the commercial strips along US-19 to the neighborhoods off Main St and Grand Blvd, New Port Richey businesses and residents are right next door to the shop. Drop off your vehicle, pick up a new sign, get a tint consultation — we\'re here.',
      local2: 'New Port Richey contractors driving US-19 and Grand Blvd pass thousands of potential customers every day. A wrapped vehicle from Fly Visuals turns every drive into a marketing opportunity — and we\'re minutes from your next job site.',
      landmarks: 'Downtown New Port Richey, Sims Park, Main St, Grand Blvd, US-19 corridor, New Port Richey City Hall, Hacienda Hotel',
      roads: 'US-19, Grand Blvd, Main St, Little Rd, SR-54',
      reviewName: 'Kevin M.', reviewInitial: 'K',
      reviews: {
        'vehicle-wraps': 'Had my plumbing van wrapped right here in New Port Richey at Fly Visuals. Drives US-19 every day and I\'ve picked up more new customers from the wrap than from any other advertising I\'ve done. Quality is unmatched and turnaround was fast.',
        'auto-tinting': 'Got ceramic tint from Fly Visuals right here in NPR — dropped off in the morning, picked up same day. The heat reduction driving US-19 is incredible. Perfect install, zero bubbles. Easy to work with.',
        'business-signs': 'Fly Visuals made our storefront sign for our New Port Richey business on US-19. It looks incredible and foot traffic increased within the first week. Quick turnaround and the design was exactly what we envisioned.',
        'boat-wraps': 'Got my boat wrapped at Fly Visuals in New Port Richey — marine-grade vinyl, flawless install, and the design is stunning. Run the Gulf regularly and the wrap handles salt and sun perfectly. Everyone at the ramp wants to know who did it.',
        'residential-tinting': 'Had Fly Visuals tint my New Port Richey home — being so close to the shop made it incredibly easy. The solar heat rejection is significant and the install was professional and clean. Couldn\'t be happier.'
      }
    },
    {
      id: 'port-richey',
      name: 'Port Richey',
      county: 'Pasco County',
      excludeServices: [],
      blurb: 'A coastal Pasco County city adjacent to New Port Richey — Port Richey businesses and residents are minutes from the Fly Visuals shop on Cormel St.',
      intro: 'Port Richey is minutes from the Fly Visuals shop on Cormel St — making it one of our closest service communities. Port Richey businesses and residents get fast turnaround and local service for vehicle wraps, signs, graphics, and window tinting without a long drive.',
      local1: 'From the US-19 commercial corridor running through Port Richey to the waterfront neighborhoods along the Gulf, local businesses need branding that holds up in Florida\'s coastal climate. Fly Visuals is right here and specs every job for Pasco County conditions.',
      local2: 'Port Richey contractors and service businesses driving US-19 and Ridge Rd are already in front of thousands of potential customers every day. A wrap from Fly Visuals makes every drive count — and we\'re close enough that dropping off a vehicle is never an inconvenience.',
      landmarks: 'Port Richey waterfront, US-19 corridor, Ridge Rd, Richey Suncoast Theatre, Port Richey Park',
      roads: 'US-19, Ridge Rd, Grand Blvd, SR-52',
      reviewName: 'Angela B.', reviewInitial: 'A',
      reviews: {
        'vehicle-wraps': 'Had my HVAC van wrapped at Fly Visuals — being right here in Port Richey, the drop-off was easy and turnaround was fast. The wrap looks sharp on US-19 every day and I\'ve gotten multiple new calls from people who saw the van. Great local shop.',
        'auto-tinting': 'Got my truck tinted at Fly Visuals — just minutes from Port Richey. Ceramic film, fast appointment, and the heat reduction on US-19 is dramatic. Perfect install and great service. Highly recommend.',
        'residential-tinting': 'Had Fly Visuals tint my Port Richey home — the west-facing rooms were brutal in summer. The film cut the heat significantly and the install was professional and clean. Couldn\'t be happier with the results.',
        'boat-wraps': 'Had my center console wrapped by Fly Visuals — living in Port Richey near the Gulf, the marine-grade vinyl they use is the right call. Handles salt and UV perfectly. The design is exactly what I wanted and the install is flawless.'
      }
    },
    {
      id: 'trinity',
      name: 'Trinity',
      county: 'Pasco County',
      excludeServices: [],
      blurb: 'An upscale Pasco County community west of Wesley Chapel — Trinity\'s growing residential and commercial base drives strong demand for professional vehicle wraps and signs.',
      intro: 'Trinity is one of Pasco County\'s most established and upscale planned communities — home to a mix of high-end residential neighborhoods and growing commercial activity along SR-54 and Little Rd. Fly Visuals serves Trinity businesses and residents with professional vehicle wraps, signs, graphics, and window tinting that match the quality standards this community expects.',
      local1: 'From the communities of Starkey Ranch and Longleaf to the commercial corridors at Trinity Town Center and along SR-54, Trinity businesses are competing in a high-expectation market. A professionally wrapped vehicle or well-made sign from Fly Visuals positions your brand where it belongs.',
      local2: 'Trinity\'s proximity to the SR-54/Little Rd corridor means your wrapped vehicle or sign is in front of Pasco County\'s highest-traffic suburban roads every day. Fly Visuals is a short drive from Trinity and handles vehicle wrap, sign, and tinting projects for Trinity customers regularly.',
      landmarks: 'Trinity Town Center, Seven Springs Golf Club, Trinity Crossings, Starkey Ranch, Longleaf, East Lake Rd corridor',
      roads: 'SR-54, Little Rd, Gunn Hwy, Starkey Rd, Seven Springs Blvd',
      reviewName: 'Jeff P.', reviewInitial: 'J',
      reviews: {
        'vehicle-wraps': 'Wrapped my real estate vehicle through Fly Visuals — driving Trinity\'s SR-54 corridor every day. My clients notice it immediately and it gives me instant credibility. The design is sharp, install is flawless, and turnaround was within the week. Excellent shop.',
        'auto-tinting': 'Got ceramic tint from Fly Visuals for my SUV — living in Trinity, the heat and glare on Little Rd was brutal. Ceramic film made a dramatic difference immediately. Fast appointment, perfect install.',
        'residential-tinting': 'Had Fly Visuals tint the windows on my Trinity home. The west-facing glass was letting in serious afternoon heat. The solar film has made the living areas comfortable all day and my A/C usage dropped noticeably.',
        'business-signs': 'Had Fly Visuals make our storefront signage for our Trinity business. The sign looks polished and upscale — which matters in this market. Customers specifically mentioned the sign as what caught their attention.'
      }
    },
    {
      id: 'odessa',
      name: 'Odessa',
      county: 'Hillsborough County',
      excludeServices: [],
      blurb: 'An affluent Tampa Bay suburb on the Hillsborough/Pasco border — Odessa\'s upscale residential communities and active commercial corridors make it a key market for wraps and signs.',
      intro: 'Odessa sits on the border of Hillsborough and Pasco counties — an affluent, well-established suburban community with a strong mix of high-end residential neighborhoods and active commercial corridors along Gunn Hwy and Veterans Expressway. Fly Visuals serves Odessa businesses and residents with professional vehicle wraps, signs, graphics, and window tinting.',
      local1: 'From the communities of Keystone and Cheval to the commercial activity along Gunn Hwy and Race Track Rd, Odessa is a competitive market where professional branding matters. A wrap from Fly Visuals positions your business as an established, trustworthy operation the moment a potential customer sees your vehicle.',
      local2: 'Odessa contractors and service businesses on Gunn Hwy, Race Track Rd, and Veterans Expressway are driving in front of dense suburban traffic every day. Fly Visuals turns that daily driving into continuous brand exposure — no recurring cost, just results.',
      landmarks: 'Keystone, Cheval, Gunn Hwy corridor, Veterans Expressway, Race Track Rd, Lake Keystone',
      roads: 'Gunn Hwy, Veterans Expressway, Race Track Rd, SR-54, Sheldon Rd',
      reviewName: 'Mark S.', reviewInitial: 'M',
      reviews: {
        'vehicle-wraps': 'Had my two work vans wrapped by Fly Visuals for my Odessa landscaping business. They drive Gunn Hwy and Veterans Expressway every day and I\'ve gotten a noticeable uptick in calls since the wraps went on. Professional install, fast turnaround, great design.',
        'auto-tinting': 'Got ceramic window tint from Fly Visuals — driving in Odessa with the Florida sun reflecting off the suburbs is brutal. The ceramic film made an immediate difference. Perfect install, no bubbles, and easy to schedule.',
        'residential-tinting': 'Fly Visuals tinted my Odessa home and the heat and glare reduction is incredible. The afternoon sun through the west windows was intense — now it\'s completely manageable. Professional crew, clean install, one day in and out.'
      }
    },
    {
      id: 'spring-hill',
      name: 'Spring Hill',
      county: 'Hernando County',
      excludeServices: [],
      blurb: 'A large Hernando County community just north of Pasco — Spring Hill\'s growing commercial base and dense residential population make it a key market for wraps, signs, and tinting.',
      intro: 'Spring Hill is Hernando County\'s largest unincorporated community — a sprawling residential and commercial area just north of Pasco County, with active commercial corridors along US-19 and Mariner Blvd. Fly Visuals serves Spring Hill businesses and residents with professional vehicle wraps, signs, graphics, and window tinting built for Florida\'s climate.',
      local1: 'From the commercial strips along US-19 and Mariner Blvd to Spring Hill\'s established neighborhoods, there\'s a growing demand for quality vehicle branding and signage. Fly Visuals is a reasonable drive from Spring Hill and serves Hernando County customers regularly.',
      local2: 'Spring Hill contractors and service businesses driving US-19 and Mariner Blvd cover a lot of ground across Hernando and north Pasco County. A wrapped vehicle from Fly Visuals means every mile doubles as advertising — building brand awareness across the communities you serve every single day.',
      landmarks: 'Mariner Blvd corridor, US-19 corridor, Weeki Wachee Springs, Spring Hill Town Center, Brookridge',
      roads: 'US-19, Mariner Blvd, Spring Hill Dr, Cortez Blvd',
      reviewName: 'Dana H.', reviewInitial: 'D',
      reviews: {
        'vehicle-wraps': 'Drove from Spring Hill to Fly Visuals for a full vehicle wrap for my contracting business — absolutely worth it. The install is perfect and driving US-19 and Mariner Blvd every day, I\'ve gotten more new customer calls than from any other advertising. Great shop.',
        'auto-tinting': 'Had Fly Visuals install ceramic tint on my truck — driving US-19 from Spring Hill daily, the heat was relentless. The ceramic film is a game changer. Clean install, done in a few hours, and the heat rejection is incredible.',
        'boat-wraps': 'Got my boat wrapped at Fly Visuals — run out of the Weeki Wachee area and the marine-grade vinyl has held up perfectly through salt, sun, and hard use. Everyone at the ramp wants to know who did it. Drive from Spring Hill is worth it every time.',
        'residential-tinting': 'Had Fly Visuals tint my Spring Hill home. The summer heat through the south and west windows was brutal — the solar film cut it significantly. Professional install, done in a day, and my A/C is noticeably less stressed.'
      }
    }
