  const cityServiceContent = {
    'wesley-chapel': {
      'vehicle-wraps': {
        h2: 'Vehicle Wraps in Wesley Chapel, FL',
        body: `Wesley Chapel is one of the fastest-growing markets in Florida — and if you run a business here, you already know how competitive it is. New businesses open every month along SR-56, the Wiregrass area, and the Bruce B Downs corridor. A professionally wrapped vehicle is one of the fastest ways to build brand recognition in a market that's still defining itself. Before a competitor gets established in your neighborhood, a wrapped truck driving past The Grove at Wesley Chapel or parked at a jobsite in Seven Oaks has already introduced your brand to hundreds of potential customers.

We wrap vehicles for Wesley Chapel contractors, tradesmen, real estate agents, home service companies, and personal vehicle owners every week. The I-75 corridor and SR-56 are some of the highest-traffic roads in Pasco County — your wrapped vehicle on those roads every day is generating thousands of impressions without any recurring cost.

Fly Visuals is based in New Port Richey, about 20 minutes from Wesley Chapel, and we serve the entire Wesley Chapel market with 3M and Avery Dennison certified vehicle wraps. Full wraps, partial wraps, color changes, and custom business advertising wraps — all designed, printed, and installed in-house.`,
        faq: [
          { q: 'How far is Fly Visuals from Wesley Chapel?', a: 'We\'re about 20 minutes from Wesley Chapel — a quick trip down SR-54 or I-75 to New Port Richey. Most customers drop off in the morning and pick up their wrapped vehicle within 2 to 4 days. We\'ve wrapped hundreds of vehicles for Wesley Chapel customers and the drive is well worth the result.' },
          { q: 'What kind of businesses in Wesley Chapel wrap their vehicles?', a: 'Wesley Chapel\'s booming growth means a huge range of service businesses are competing for the same customers. We wrap vehicles for HVAC companies, landscapers, pool service, pest control, real estate agents, electricians, plumbers, cleaning services, and contractors all across the Wesley Chapel market. The businesses that get wrapped consistently tell us they generate more calls and close more jobs because of the professional image a wrap creates.' }
