      },
      'fleet-wraps': {
        h2: 'Fleet Wraps for Wesley Chapel Businesses',
        body: `Wesley Chapel is growing faster than almost any other market in Florida right now — which means competition for local customers is intense. If you run a fleet-based service business along the SR-56 corridor, Bruce B Downs, or anywhere in the Wesley Chapel area, consistent fleet branding is one of the most powerful moves you can make. When a potential customer sees three vans with the same professional look driving through Wiregrass or parked in front of homes in Meadow Pointe, it registers as an established, trusted operation. That's what fleet wraps do.

Fly Visuals handles fleet wrap projects for Wesley Chapel businesses of all sizes — from 2 vans to 20+ vehicles. We offer volume pricing that gets better the more vehicles you wrap, and we stagger installations so your operation never loses too many vehicles at once. Every vehicle gets the same design, the same colors, the same quality — brand consistency across your entire fleet from the first van to the last.`,
        faq: [
          { q: 'Do I have to bring all my fleet vehicles at once?', a: 'No — and for most Wesley Chapel businesses that would be impractical anyway. We schedule fleet installations in batches based on your operation\'s needs. Bring a couple of vehicles at a time, keep the rest running, and we work through the fleet on a timeline that keeps your business moving. It\'s how we handle most fleet jobs for Pasco County businesses.' },
          { q: 'Does fleet pricing make sense for a small fleet in Wesley Chapel?', a: 'Fleet pricing starts at 2 vehicles and the savings per vehicle are real even at small quantities. For a Wesley Chapel service business running 2 or 3 vans on the SR-56 corridor every day, getting both wrapped at once vs. one at a time saves money and delivers a more consistent look across your fleet immediately.' }
        ]
      },
      'auto-tinting': {
        h2: 'Ceramic Window Tint in Wesley Chapel, FL',
        body: `<p>Wesley Chapel gets serious heat bouncing off the SR-56 and SR-54 retail corridors all summer. Ceramic tint blocks the infrared at the glass before it ever heats up your cabin — meaning your AC isn't fighting the sun, your seats aren't burning, and your dashboard isn't cracking from UV. We install Madico and LLumar ceramic film exclusively — no dyed film, no carbon, no film that purples or bubbles in Florida's climate.</p><p>We serve drivers from Wiregrass Ranch, Estancia, Pebble Creek, New Tampa, and across the Wesley Chapel area. Most auto tint jobs are done same-day or next-day at our Port Richey shop.</p>`,
        faq: [
          { q: 'Is ceramic tint worth it for Wesley Chapel summers?', a: 'Absolutely — and Wesley Chapel drivers who commute on I-75 or sit in traffic on SR-56 every day feel the difference most. Ceramic tint rejects the infrared heat that dyed and carbon films let through, so your car stays meaningfully cooler even when parked in direct sun at a Wesley Chapel shopping center all day. Most customers tell us they noticed the difference within the first week.' },
          { q: 'What tint shades are popular in Wesley Chapel?', a: '35% on the front side windows is very popular with Wesley Chapel customers who want heat rejection and glare reduction without a heavily darkened appearance. 20% on the rear windows gives more privacy and is the standard for many SUVs and trucks. We\'ll help you find the right shade combination that looks great on your specific vehicle.' }
        ]
      },
      'boat-wraps': {
        h2: 'Boat Wraps Near Wesley Chapel, FL',
        body: `Wesley Chapel is inland but plenty of residents boat on local lakes — Callaway Lake, Lake Crenshaw, and the lakes in the surrounding Pasco County area — and many make the short drive to Gulf access at Hudson Beach or the Pithlachascotee River in New Port Richey. If you're a Wesley Chapel boater who wants a custom wrap for your bass boat, pontoon, or any other vessel, Fly Visuals in New Port Richey is your closest professional marine wrap shop.

We use marine-grade vinyl specifically engineered for saltwater and UV exposure — the same conditions your boat faces whether you're running local lakes or heading out to the Gulf from Hudson or Tarpon Springs. Tournament wraps, hull graphics, boat name and registration numbers, full hull color changes — we do all of it for boaters from the Wesley Chapel area and across Pasco County.`,
        faq: [
          { q: 'Can Wesley Chapel boaters use Fly Visuals for boat wraps?', a: 'Absolutely — we\'re about 20 minutes from Wesley Chapel and we wrap boats for customers from all over Pasco County and beyond. If you boat local lakes or make weekend trips to Hudson Beach or the Gulf, we can wrap your vessel with marine-grade vinyl that handles whatever Florida waters throw at it. Call or fill out the form for a free quote.' },
          { q: 'How long does a boat wrap last on Florida lakes and Gulf water?', a: 'With proper marine-grade vinyl, 3 to 5 years is typical even in Florida\'s harsh UV environment. Lake boaters in the Wesley Chapel area may see slightly longer life than Gulf boaters due to less saltwater exposure, but the UV load is similar. We use UV-resistant laminate on all boat graphics to maximize longevity.' }
        ]
