      'vehicle-graphics': {
        h2: 'Vehicle Graphics for Wesley Chapel Businesses',
        body: `Vehicle graphics for Wesley Chapel businesses — door logos, hood accents, lettering, and custom printed panel graphics — are one of the most cost-effective branding investments you can make in a high-traffic market like Wesley Chapel. The SR-56 corridor, I-75, and Bruce B Downs are among the busiest roads in Pasco County, and a well-branded vehicle on those roads every day builds the kind of local recognition that takes years to build through digital advertising alone.

Fly Visuals produces and installs vehicle graphics for all types of vehicles serving the Wesley Chapel market. Cut vinyl, digitally printed graphics, full-color door panels, and lettering packages — designed in-house and installed at our New Port Richey shop.`,
        faq: [
          { q: 'What vehicle graphics do Wesley Chapel business owners order most?', a: 'For service businesses in Wesley Chapel, the most common order is a combination of door logo graphics, lettering with the business name and phone number, and a rear panel or tailgate graphic with the main service listed. Real estate agents in Wesley Chapel frequently order subtle door graphics with their headshot, name, and brokerage. Landscapers, HVAC companies, and contractors typically go for bold, high-contrast designs that read well at a distance.' },
          { q: 'How long do vehicle graphics last on Wesley Chapel roads?', a: 'Cast vinyl vehicle graphics from Fly Visuals typically last 5 to 7 years in Florida\'s climate — longer than calendered film alternatives. For vehicles driving SR-56 and I-75 every day, the UV exposure and road debris are real considerations. We use only cast vinyl and UV-resistant laminate on all vehicle graphics to maximize durability in the Wesley Chapel market.' }
